  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "If the tangent at the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;on the curve <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn></math>&nbsp;passes through the origin, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;does NOT lie on the curve",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "75VDP",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>81</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "sVmOT",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>9</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "RStFF",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "5A5cl",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math>",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn></math></p><p>Now <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>x</mi></math></p><p>So at point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mrow><mi>at</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></mfenced></math></p><p>Also slope of line in two point form will be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mi>ii</mi></mfenced></math></p><p>Also <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;lie on curve</p><p>We get <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mi>iii</mi></mfenced></math></p><p>From equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></mfenced></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>ii</mi></mfenced></math> we get <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> (as slope is&nbsp;equal)</p><p>Now <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>15</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>i.e.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow/><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>15</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp;does not intersect the curve&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p>",
